<p id="S3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This Möbius matrix <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is the inverse of the zeta matrix <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2. Triangular numbers: zeta matrix and Möbius matrix ‣ 3. Poset of triangular numbers ‣ The Möbius function of the poset of triangular numbers under divisibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
