<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Results: data on Möbius values</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we report some empirical observations concerning the values of the Möbius function <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The values are available on the Online Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences (OEIS) as sequence A350682 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Möbius values with <math id="S4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 4.1. Möbius values with 𝑚=1 ‣ 4. Results: data on Möbius values ‣ The Möbius function of the poset of triangular numbers under divisibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we show the Möbius values of the partial order <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathbb{N},\leq_{\mathcal{T}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{N},\leq_{\mathcal{T}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The values are highly erratic, rapidly switching between positive and negative values.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2402.07934v1/Mobius_Values_Graph.png" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:399/299;" width="399" height="299" alt="Refer to caption">
