<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1. </span>Inputs of the Möbius function <math id="S4.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> with increasing magnitude.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This data leads us to make the following conjecture.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmconj4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_conj">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmconj4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conjecture 4</span></span><span id="Thmconj4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmconj4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmconj4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any positive integer <math id="Thmconj4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a positive integer <math id="Thmconj4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmconj4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{|\mu_{\mathcal{T}}(n)|\geq M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{|\mu_{\mathcal{T}}(n)|\geq M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5. </span>Two-variable Möbius values</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Möbius matrices ‣ The Möbius function of the poset of triangular numbers under divisibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> we show a heatmap illustrating the values of the two-variable Möbius function for <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathbb{N},\leq_{\mathcal{T}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{N},\leq_{\mathcal{T}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This should allow further explorations for patterns in the Möbius values in future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Further questions</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If Conjecture <a href="#Thmconj1" title="Conjecture 1 (Growth of partial sums of 𝜇_𝒯). ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The Möbius function of the poset of triangular numbers under divisibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds, what are bounds on the constant <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>?
Can the exact value of <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be computed?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Other statistics to measure on <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to Conjecture  <a href="#Thmconj5" title="Conjecture 5. ‣ 5. Further questions ‣ The Möbius function of the poset of triangular numbers under divisibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, is there an asymptotic relation of the form</p>
<table id="S5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{n\to\infty}\sum^{n}_{i=1}\frac{\mu_{\mathcal{T}}(i)}{\mathcal{T}(i)}\approx D," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{n\to\infty}\sum^{n}_{i=1}\frac{\mu_{\mathcal{T}}(i)}{\mathcal{T}(i)}\approx D,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is some constant?</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmconj5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_conj">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmconj5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conjecture 5</span></span><span id="Thmconj5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmconj5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmconj5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a positive constant <math id="Thmconj5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{n\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mu_{\mathcal{T}}(i)}{i}=-E." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{n\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mu_{\mathcal{T}}(i)}{i}=-E.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This constant <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-E</annotation></semantics></math>, can be seen to be around approximately <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.239" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.239</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.239</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
